    {
      "id": "0cfcd68d30dd8a27d03152da8b09ccf5636da39c",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1280534397,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I added this:\n```c\n+\ttvbuff_t *next_tvb = tvb_new_subset_length(tvb, offset, lenstr);\n+\tadd_new_data_source(pinfo, next_tvb, \"local infile\");\n```\n\nThis shows the file. Usually these are CSV files. Usually UTF-8, but there can be actual binary in the CSV for things like binary encoded UUID's and IP's. Not sure what the best way is to display this and allow people to extract these files.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5884947,
            "username": "dveeden",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Daniël van Eeden",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/00c536bb5304097eb409787c4a770e820db2a200d04130b8ca03cbcda0f526f7?s=80&d=identicon",
