        },
        {
          "id": 1402359092,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I have some examples of a similar case, where a text row packet starts with `00` and is now incorrectly being dissected as a binary row packet. That requires more changes because right now there's no distinguishing between a text mode query and a prepared statement binary mode; it needs to track whether binary or text resultset rows are expected based on the request type.\n\nIn this case, I think that for LOCAL INFILE the current state would generally be RESPONSE TABULAR (possibly REQUEST in some odd cases), whereas for a text row packet would usually be ROW PACKET. For cases where the state is anything else I don't know how to handle it.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-05-23T18:45:23.344Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-05-23T18:45:23.344Z",
